{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And a shoot shall come forth, etc.</b> Most of the commentators say that this is the Messiah, and the meaning is that the camp of Assyria, which besieged Jerusalem, shall perish, and further, the time of the complete redemption of Jerusalem shall come. But according to the opinion of Rabbi Moses the Kohen, he hinted at Hezekiah, for it is connected with the pericope:" "<b>Ḥoter.</b> From the Aramaic translation [targum] of matteh (staff):" "<b>Gazaʿ.</b> Like zeraʿ (seed)." "<b>Ve-netzer</b> like seʿif (branch), as in netzer nitaʿav (Isaiah 14:19)." "And the meaning of <b>ve-yatza</b> (shall come forth) is that he was young when this prophecy was [given]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved הפרשה as 'the pericope' (the preceding prophetic unit); ambiguous which pericope is meant.", 4 "Bracketed variant reading היתה reflects a witness or editor's correction for feminine agreement with נבואה; translated the corrected form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:24.589896713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}